2026-10-24T10:30:32.4775049Z    image gate: kimball_house_1801_prairie taylor_c1895_northwest: verdict "differs", 8 difference(s) open: the tower's form: a shaft about 2.4 m across under a corbelled upper stage about 3.6 m across, its cone flaring from the stage; the build is one eight-sided prism 2.9 m across; the flank section stands about 0.1 m proud on the sheet; the build stands it 0.6 m proud (K08's pavilion depth, the least its window recesses fit in; the main eave's gutter, its lip 0.46 m out, also dies behind it). Its width is ruled with it (T-3001): at the built depth the build's 6.0 m (u 5.1-11.1) renders its west edge at about x 500 against the print's pilaster at x 497-501, so T-2538's 7.8 m was its camera's; at the sheet's 0.1 m the same edge falls at u 3.9 and the section would be about 7.2 m, so moving it to the sheet's depth means widening it past K08's 6.0 m. The pavilion stood 0.6 m proud too; the east turret's shaft and finial: the print shows the shaft about 15 px wider toward the front (to x 237; the build's to about x 220), a moulded band at its first floor and a heavy eave moulding, and a finial spike about 2.5 m tall over the cone's neck (y 778 to 702), where the build's stands about 0.7 m; the mansard's curb and deck: at the front's north-west corner the print's curb stands about 35-50 px lower than the build's (the corner hip's top at about x 950, y 320 against 978, 247) and its corner hip runs about 25-30 px west of the build's; the front's deck ends at the print's x 1092 under its south finial, where the build's runs on to x 1187. So the cresting, the corner hood and its finial stand about 35-50 px over the print's, and the south finial about 95 px south of it (seen by T-3000); the hooded dormers' hoods: the print's cheeks widen further up the roof than the build's (the flank's lit cheek about 45 px across at the top against the build's about 25), as its lower faces fall back faster than the build's 72 degrees do; and their faces are slate with a pale frame round the light, where the build's are stone; the gabled section's openings: the print's principal storey has three round-arched lights across the section (x 360-440), the second an oriel on corbels with a carved panel over it (x 362-435, about 5.4-8.1 m), and the third an open loggia behind the balustrade (x 382-422, its head about 11.4 m) under the gable; the build lays one mullioned and transomed pair a storey on the pavilion and its balustrade bows out where the print's runs straight; the print's pier at about u 0-0.9 (x 422-445), up to the cornice, is not built; the flank section's top: over the corbel table (about 9.5 m) the print's section carries a third storey of paired lights under a cornice, a gabled wall dormer with a finial (x 520-600) and the tall round-topped stack (x 467-530); the build carries the section's wall to 13.9 m under K08's low hip; the lights over the loggia, on the front and the flank: the print's outlines read about 1.4 m across (x 1016-1071 and 877-931 px), about 1.2 m once the lit reveal of the near jamb is taken off, against the build's 1.15 m (K01's widest ordinary sash); their transom bar stands about 0.75-1.0 m under the head where K06's transom light is 0.45 m; and each stands in a moulded frame under a projecting head between carved pilasters, where the build lays K01's flat arch
